    backlog:frozenRuling "Owner, 2026-09-07, verbatim: 'Unfreeze and let's do this appropriately with an additional benefit: prove the new method is working correctly.' Ruling: explicit unfreeze. The restart of 2026-09-07 stands (it was owner-instructed before commit 0251509; the repository could not witness that instruction, which is why the thrash was recorded and is kept). The chain of L_ChangeDiscipline is rebuilt from Mission, one stage per commit, each stage output witnessed after the previous one; the two pre-lineage items are re-admitted only by the rebuilt Stage_Backlog output. The rebuild is itself the proof of the method: at every step the order check must report the lineage in the state the ceremony predicts, and the restart loop must be seen to converge in one trial." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

