fw:Find_AP2_StatusNotAdvanced a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The lineage status stayed Opened through the Scope, Goal and Objective stages and moved only at the Backlog stage; no shape refused it and no step did it, because the status was set by hand at the end." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not repaired in this lineage. The step tool reads what a status owes, but nothing advances the status at a stage. Recorded for the successor: a probe that plants a stage output without the matching status, and a status move in the stage release." .
fw:Find_AP2_ReceiptReadAnotherRepository a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Release tool 1.6.0 looked up the head of another default repository than the publisher, so no gate receipt was written in 1.462.0 and the publisher ran the gate again (349 s). Found afterwards, from one log line." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Release tool 1.7.0 reads the repository from the publisher's own script; the speed probe shows the receipt written, valid and invalid." .
fw:Find_AP2_RegisterNotValidatedByGate a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The gate was run without an argument by the release tool and the publisher, so its register section never ran and release 1.461.0 was published with a Mission that named no outcome; found five hours later by validating by hand." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Gate 1.73.0 validates the newest register by itself; the preflight validates it too." .
fw:Find_AP2_GeneratorDoubledName a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "A scope generator written by text replacement from the previous lineage's generator doubled a name; it was found by the new preflight in seconds, which is the case the preflight was built for." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Recorded; generate from the lineage name as a parameter, not by replacement." .
fw:Find_AP2_ReportRunLeaked a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The roadmap-report run recorded at a box opening was kept as reference by the validator while the register typing it reports on was dropped, so the positive fixture violated; release 1.468.0 was refused at the gate ten minutes in. A box opening had never been recorded into a published register before, so the fault was latent." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Validator 1.18.0 treats report runs as register statements; the preflight validates the positive fixture; the reference probe holds it." .
fw:Find_AP2_ToolsBeforeScope a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "At the Owner's order (an urgent cost risk) the tools were built before the Scope stage was released; the Scope records were set aside and re-added, and release 1.462.0 was lost to an interrupt of a background run." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Start a release detached so that an interrupt does not end it; the order was disclosed and the chain was not bypassed." .
fw:Find_AP2_NoteNamesRulingByIdentifier a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "A checkpoint note written by hand named a ruling by its identifier, which is text where a link belongs; the link-control probe refused the preflight of release 1.469.0." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "The note was reworded. Not repaired in the tool: a later version of the step tool should refuse an identifier-like word in a note." .
fw:Find_AP2_OpenRefusedAfterToolChange a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Box 2 could not be opened because the step tool had already been renamed in the tree (work before the box), and the tool refused as designed; the published bytes had to be restored to open it." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Open the box before any change to the tool the box uses; the refusal was correct and was kept." .
fw:Find_AP2_StageReleaseBlockedByOpenBox a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "A box opened in a release of its own would let the lineage-order check see the plan before the work (box 1 and box 2 draw PLANNED_LATE), but the plan names a deployment unit that the tool creates only at the close, so the archive integrity check refuses the half-open register." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not repaired. The step tool should create the deployment unit when it opens a box and complete it at the close; recorded for the successor." .
fw:Find_AP2_ReleaseCountAndTime a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_AP2_BoxesJudged ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Lineage 22 needed eight published releases and three refused attempts for five stage outputs and three boxes. Of the gate failures, three were found by the gate after ten to thirty minutes and one by the preflight in seconds; the rest of the time went to the one-commit-per-stage rule and to tools that read the same files again inside loops." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Release tool 1.6.0 to 1.9.0 (preflight of the register, fixture, digests, archive integrity and link control), the light gate for stage releases, the keyed gate and three removed over-processing faults. The gate of a real release fell from 724 s to 401 s; the total from 17 to 20 minutes to 9." .
