#################################################################
#  v1.470.0 -- LINEAGE 22 closure: the mission is achieved, measured by its nine objectives.
#################################################################

fw:CR_AdaptiveProof2 a backlog:ClosureReport ;
    backlog:closesForMission fw:Mission_AdaptiveProof2 ;
    backlog:reportGeneratedAt "2026-10-30T01:50:47Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasClosureSummary "The mission asked that a lineage run under the revised adaptive profile carry real work from an immature mission to a closure, its boxes recorded in order by the step tool and judged by the rules it adopted, with the checks that judge archived and live lineages in agreement and what the first application left undone done. Measured by the nine objectives, all at target: scope deliverables with no satisfying item Done 7 to 0; archived lineages failing only because the check reads another digest table 1 to 0 (adapted: the premise was false, the cause is now measured); subject forms the archive tool leaves behind 1 to 0; tool commands applying obligations from code unchecked 2 to 0; boxes not closed with the step tool and clean 3 to 0; opt-in rule sets with no recorded decision 8 to 0 (ten decided, one included in profile revision 9); post-mortems missing 1 to 0; rule-set inclusions of the standard and agentic profiles lost 0 held. The gate objective went from 629 s to 184 s in a full gate run on the final tree after a record was added to the register; the real releases of the lineage took 401 s (1.469.0, a release that changed tools) after 724 s in 1.468.0, and the stage releases 144 s each; a release that only adds records was not measured in a real release, and the figure of 184 s is that of the run described. What is not claimed: the post-mortem was written by the agent that did the work and was not reviewed by an independent one; the adaptive profile is not the default and the Owner has not confirmed that it should become one; three faults are recorded as not repaired (the lineage status is not advanced at each stage, the step tool does not create the deployment unit when it opens a box, the validator costs about 7.6 s per planted scenario)." ;
    backlog:reportsOnObjective fw:Obj_AP2_MissionMet , fw:Obj_AP2_Digest , fw:Obj_AP2_Forms , fw:Obj_AP2_Step , fw:Obj_AP2_Boxes , fw:Obj_AP2_Profile , fw:Obj_AP2_Gate , fw:Obj_AP2_PostMortem , fw:Obj_AP2_Contained ;
    backlog:citesFinding fw:Find_AP2_D1Premise , fw:Find_AP2_GeneratorDoubledName , fw:Find_AP2_NoteNamesRulingByIdentifier , fw:Find_AP2_OpenRefusedAfterToolChange , fw:Find_AP2_OverProcessing , fw:Find_AP2_PlannedLate , fw:Find_AP2_ProbeCost , fw:Find_AP2_ReceiptReadAnotherRepository , fw:Find_AP2_RegisterNotValidatedByGate , fw:Find_AP2_ReleaseCountAndTime , fw:Find_AP2_ReportRunLeaked , fw:Find_AP2_StageReleaseBlockedByOpenBox , fw:Find_AP2_StatusNotAdvanced , fw:Find_AP2_StepToolCarriedObligations , fw:Find_AP2_ToolsBeforeScope , fw:Find_AP2_UndeclaredPredicate , fw:Find_AP2_ValidationRanWithoutRegister ;
    backlog:statesBestPractice "Time a check inside its section before writing a rule about releases: three of the slowest checks of the gate spent most of their time reading the same files again in a loop, and a profile of each cost minutes where the rule would have cost weeks." ,
        "Run in the preflight, in seconds, every check that the gate would refuse a release for after ten minutes: each refusal of this lineage after the first was a check the preflight did not yet run." ,
        "Measure a premise before it is written into a deliverable: the first deliverable of this lineage rested on a cause that the measurement showed to be wrong, and was kept in an adapted form with the reason recorded." .

# ---- Lineage 23: opening and Mission stage ----
