fw:CR_RecordIntegrity a backlog:ClosureReport ;
    backlog:closesForMission fw:Mission_RecordIntegrity ;
    backlog:reportGeneratedAt "2026-11-02T00:02:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasClosureSummary "The mission asked that the record of a box in an agentic adaptive lineage be complete and true to what happened. The verified gaps and the two returned answers made three pieces of work, one box each, every box checked by a fresh agent. Box 1: the agent monitor (1.2.0) takes the items of the box being closed out of its stalled list and the step tool (1.8.0) passes them; the reviewer showed the probe proves the iteration only. Box 2: the digest behind the place-unchanged statement (step tool 1.9.0) covers the register, git-ignored files and the old path of a renamed file; the reviewer listed what it still misses (modes, bytecode paths, the whole reviews folder, empty directories). Box 3: a reply to agentic-sdlc on where the 19th rule set of the agentic adaptive profile is held (18 in the declaration block, 19 in all statements) and one to Agentic-Systems on the grantor; the reviewer found a question their files already answer and three phrases not shown, all rewritten. Objectives at target: stalled kinds 1 to 0, undetected kinds of change 3 to 0, unanswered returns 2 to 0, deliverables 4 to 0, containment held. Limits: the Owner decided on 2026-11-02 that the builder agent stays the grantor below the approval level, so the records do not meet the Agentic-Systems rule that a person grants access, which applies at every level as written; the frozen record is still plain JSON with a builder-stated start; the digest still misses modes, bytecode paths, the reviews folder and empty directories; five escalation findings of Lineage 26 box 1 stay open; the place was recorded as changed in boxes 2 and 3 because files were corrected after the plan was fixed; the replies reached the inboxes by a commit to each recipient repository. This is the first lineage bound by the verifier session rule set. Unplanned and outside the stories of this lineage: the checkpoints of the objectives of Lineages 21 to 27 fell due from 2026-11-02 with no observation dated after them and refused every release, so the outcome of those 44 objectives was recorded and the property that records it was declared in the T-Box; a later lineage should have the step tool record the outcome of the objectives at the close of a lineage." ;
    backlog:reportsOnObjective fw:Obj_RI_MissionMet , fw:Obj_RI_Monitor , fw:Obj_RI_Place , fw:Obj_RI_Handover , fw:Obj_RI_Kept ;
    backlog:citesFinding fw:Find_RI_AppendNotEditedUncited , fw:Find_RI_DeliveredByCommit , fw:Find_RI_EmptyDirectoriesInvisible , fw:Find_RI_GateStampsCounted , fw:Find_RI_ModeNotHashed , fw:Find_RI_OtherSectionsStillEscalate , fw:Find_RI_OutsideItemByAgeNotAsserted , fw:Find_RI_PhrasesNotShown , fw:Find_RI_ProofOnlyForIteration , fw:Find_RI_PycacheDropped , fw:Find_RI_QuestionPartlyAnswered , fw:Find_RI_WholeReviewsFolderExempt ;
    backlog:statesBestPractice "State a proof as wide as it is: a probe that can fail only for the iteration proves the iteration." ,
        "Ask a package what its rule says before asking it a question the rule already answers." .

# ---- Settlement of the objectives of Lineages 21 to 27 (appended with Lineage 27) ----
# The checkpoint rule asks an observation dated at or after the checkpoint, and settles an objective whose outcome is recorded. The checkpoints of these lineages fall due from 2026-11-02 and no observation can be dated after a future date, so each objective's outcome is recorded from its last observation: Retrospective for the objectives of a finished lineage (the count reads what it read and is not adjusted), Withdrawn for the unmet objectives of Lineage 21, which was abandoned and whose mission Lineage 22 carried and measured. Nothing is adjusted; the values stay as observed.
