fw:Mission_PlannedDates a backlog:Mission ;
    backlog:hasMissionOutcome backlog:Out_Achieved ;
    backlog:outcomeRationale "Achieved as worded, on three boxes, each checked by a fresh agent. A checkpoint date of a lineage that adopts planned dates rests on its own forecast (shape and tool, box 1); every box gets a base plan with a predicted end and the objectives it moves are checked against it (box 2); the base, updated and finished dates of every objective and box are reported with their variances (box 3). Not claimed: that a forecast was discussed with the Owner before the dates were final (nothing records it), that the shapes have fired on real data (Lineage 28 was opened under profile revision 11 and is not bound by them), that the pace of past boxes predicts the next, or that the report copes with malformed records (it trusts a validated register)." ; rdfs:label "Mission: every measure date of a lineage comes from its plan"@en ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Every measure date of a lineage comes from its plan: predicted at planning from the scope, the work and the capacity of the agents, shown for discussion before it is final, kept as a base plan, updated when the sprint tasks are matched to the objectives, and reported as base, updated and finished dates." ;
    backlog:missionFor fw:Register ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin backlog:Origin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:missionSource "Owner, 2026-11-02 10:22: a measure date is set at planning, not ad hoc to satisfy a goal on time; when an agent sets none, a prediction from scope, work and capacity is made and discussed before it is final; after the work is planned into sprints the dates are updated; the base plan, the updated and the finished dates are reported. Gaps verified: no plan baseline, forecast or planned finish exists in the register and the checkpoint dates of Lineages 21 to 27 were stated by the builder and fell due with no observation after them." ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Mission_PlannedDates ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
