# Lineage 29, box 2: the ways to clear each kind of obstacle (G190)
backlog:Mth_SatisfyInStep a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Satisfy the obligation in the same step"@en ;
    skos:definition "Read the refusal, do what the rule asks in the step it refused, run the check again. Gone when the same check passes without a change to the rule."@en .
backlog:Mth_RedoInOrder a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Redo the steps in the order the discipline gives"@en ;
    skos:definition "List the steps of the stage in the order the discipline states, undo or redo, in the files already changed, the steps done early or late, then run the checks. Gone when the order check passes."@en .
backlog:Mth_ChangeThroughManagement a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Change the rule through change management"@en ;
    skos:definition "Only when the rule contradicts the mission or the facts (shown by a case in which it refuses correct work, kept as a probe case): raise a change request that supports the mission, get the ruling and shape changed as a new version, then continue under it. Gone when the new version is published; the rule is never skipped meanwhile."@en .
backlog:Mth_FreshAgentReview a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Have a fresh agent review the claim"@en ;
    skos:definition "Give an agent that did not do the work the brief and the files, and let it check the claim. Gone when its review is in the package and the claim stands or is corrected."@en .
backlog:Mth_KeepRecordInPackage a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Keep the record in the package"@en ;
    skos:definition "Move the evidence (a figure, a test drive, a review) from where it lived into the package, as a file or a register record the reader can open. Gone when a reader can check it from the package alone."@en .
backlog:Mth_StateTheLimit a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "State the limit plainly"@en ;
    skos:definition "Write what could not be shown or reached, why, and what the claim therefore does not cover, in the record where the claim is made. Gone when the claim no longer says more than the evidence."@en .
backlog:Mth_ReproduceAndRepairTool a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Reproduce the fault, then repair the tool as a new version"@en ;
    skos:definition "Run the tool on the smallest input that fails, write that input as a probe case, repair the tool as a new version, run the probe. Gone when the probe passes and the old failing run is fixed."@en .
backlog:Mth_AskOwnerOneQuestion a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Ask the Owner one question"@en ;
    skos:definition "Put one question in plain words with two or three options and what each leads to, at the step where it is needed. Gone when the Owner answers and the answer is recorded."@en .
backlog:Mth_DecideByRule a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Decide by the rule when the facts settle it"@en ;
    skos:definition "Read the rule or the facts that bear on the choice; when they settle it, take the choice and record the rule it rests on. Gone when the decision is recorded with its basis. Not used when the rules leave the choice open."@en .
backlog:Mth_AskForTheFile a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Ask for the file or the access"@en ;
    skos:definition "Say which file or access is needed, where it is expected, and why; ask the person who holds it to attach it. Gone when it arrives."@en .
backlog:Mth_UseAllowedRoute a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Use a route that is allowed"@en ;
    skos:definition "Find another route to the same thing that the limits allow (another tool, the installed package, a fresh fetch through the ceremony); never go round the limit itself. Gone when the thing is reached by that route."@en .
backlog:Mth_BoundedRetry a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Retry a bounded number of times"@en ;
    skos:definition "Repeat the call three times at most, pausing a minute longer each time, and stop at the bound. Gone when a call succeeds; when the bound is reached the obstacle is not cleared and the next method applies."@en .
backlog:Mth_RestartTheChain a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Restart the chain from the stage that was skipped"@en ;
    skos:definition "Never backfill a bypassed stage: open the chain again from the stage that was skipped, one commit per stage. Gone when the stages exist in order."@en .
backlog:Mth_ReorderTheBox a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Reorder the work of the box"@en ;
    skos:definition "Before the work is recorded, put the steps planned for the box in the order its rules need (open, plan, freeze, review, close). Gone when the box closes without a refusal for order."@en .
backlog:Imp_RuleRefusal backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_SatisfyInStep .
backlog:Imp_RuleRefusal backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_RedoInOrder .
backlog:Imp_RuleRefusal backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_ChangeThroughManagement .
backlog:Imp_EvidenceGap backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_FreshAgentReview .
backlog:Imp_EvidenceGap backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_KeepRecordInPackage .
backlog:Imp_EvidenceGap backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_StateTheLimit .
backlog:Imp_ToolFault backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_ReproduceAndRepairTool .
backlog:Imp_WrongOrder backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_RestartTheChain .
backlog:Imp_WrongOrder backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_ReorderTheBox .
backlog:Imp_WrongOrder backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_RedoInOrder .
backlog:Imp_AccessLimit backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_AskForTheFile .
backlog:Imp_AccessLimit backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_UseAllowedRoute .
backlog:Imp_AccessLimit backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_StateTheLimit .
backlog:Imp_DecisionWaiting backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_AskOwnerOneQuestion .
backlog:Imp_DecisionWaiting backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_DecideByRule .
backlog:Imp_ServiceFailure backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_BoundedRetry .
fw:Ruling_G190 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G190" ;
    rdfs:label "An obstacle is cleared by a known way that keeps every rule"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "Each of the seven kinds of obstacle lists the ways known to clear it (fourteen ways in all, none of which waives, skips or defers an obligation: each satisfies it, redoes the work in order, changes the rule through change management, or states the limit). An impediment that is cleared names the way used, and the way is one its kind lists. A way is advice about what to try, not an order: the work may use another way once it is added to the kind." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:ClearedImpedimentNamesMethodShape , backlog:KindHasMethodShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_OPERATING_DISCIPLINE v154.0.0, section G190; Owner direction of 2026-11-02 10:35." .
fw:Ruling_G190 backlog:rulingDecides backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown .
