fw:Find_IK_ToolReviewRounds a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_RaiseAdviseClear ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The first three reviews rejected the box: the tool wrote invalid text for a newline in a statement or an odd prefix, refused every real item, could be emptied by text that is not valid UTF-8, lost writes made together, left a register broken when a write stopped partway, let two clears of one impediment both through, and a statement quoting a later number blocked it; the probe's final check could not fail; the clearing time of the real record was the time of the release, not of the repair; the ruling named shapes for more than they hold." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Repaired and reviewed again, four times: the tool encodes first, writes under a lock without a buffer, cuts a failed write back exactly, parses the register again and restores it, checks a clear under the lock and a number by type; the probe has a control and cases for each fault; the time and the ruling were corrected. The fourth reviewer found nothing serious left." .
fw:Find_IK_ReleasePreflightMissesVocabulary a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_RaiseAdviseClear ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The release preflight does not run the vocabulary probe, so the fourteen ways, added to the register without being listed by the T-Box, were refused by the gate 37 minutes into the release of 3.7.0 (the first obstacle entered with the tool, cleared in ten minutes)." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not repaired in this box: the preflight of the release tool should run the vocabulary probe, as it already runs the link-control probe; a change for the release tool." .
fw:Find_IK_RealRecordEnteredAfterTheFact a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_RaiseAdviseClear ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The one real impediment of the lineage was met before the tool was written and entered with the tool afterwards with given times (the refusal from the release log, the repair from the backup); it blocks a story already finished and stands between two boxes, so the dates report places it in none; the register cannot tell it from a live entry." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Disclosed in the record and the narrative; not repairable, the next obstacle is entered when it is met." .
fw:Find_IK_ToolAcceptedAndUnscoped a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_RaiseAdviseClear ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The tool accepts a block on an item of another lineage or on one already Done, and a person, run or mission as the blocked thing; the monitor and the report count an impediment only through its own link to the lineage; the report skips an impediment with no raise time without naming it; a duplicate number written by hand with a prefixed address would slip past the check." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not repaired in this box; stated in the narrative." .
fw:Find_IK_CatalogueGapsLeftAtClosure a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_RaiseAdviseClear ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The gaps found in the catalogue by the reviews of boxes 1 and 2 were not repaired: three findings are placed in a kind they do not fit; evidence missing has no way that supplies the evidence and an outside service failing has only a bounded retry; the three ways for work in the wrong order disagree about editing recorded files; the resolved time is not checked as a date after the raise on hand-written records; asking the Owner is listed before deciding by the rule with no gate." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not repaired in this lineage: the catalogue is advice and the repairs are a change to the register of the next lineage that touches it; the closure report states them as not achieved." .
