    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Reproduced on 2026-11-02: backlog_date_report v1.1.0 on a copy of the register with one checkpoint date replaced by text stops with a TypeError comparing a date with nothing. The lineage's own finding says \"Not repaired in this box\". Genuine gap." .

# ---- Reactivation of Lineage 29, 2026-11-02 (Owner decision of 2026-11-03 01:34 Istanbul) ----
# The status pointer of Lineage 29 moved in place from Achieved to Revived, as the pointer rule requires; this record and git keep what it was.
fw:React_C29 a backlog:LineageReactivation ; rdfs:label "Reactivation of Lineage 29: its mission was not accomplished"@en ;
    backlog:reactivatesLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasReactivationReason backlog:Reason_NonConformantResult ;
    backlog:addressesFinding fw:Find_C29_NoLiveProof ;
    backlog:reactivationRationale "The mission of Lineage 29 is that a blocked agent can name, record and clear an obstacle. It was closed Achieved on the lineage's own proxy counts; no obstacle was ever raised live in a box, so the result does not conform to the mission as worded. The Owner chose, on 2026-11-03, to revive this lineage and finish its unfinished work in it, with no second lineage; the other gaps, bounded and isolated, are worked inside it. The chain is rebuilt from the objective stage so that the lineage adopts the current rule sets." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

# ---- Ruling G192, 2026-11-03: a revived lineage opens again where its chain is rebuilt ----
fw:Ruling_G192 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G192" ;
    rdfs:label "A revived lineage opens again at the commit of its latest stage revision, and may adopt the current rule sets there"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A lineage that was revived (lineageRevivedAt, with a reactivation that names it) and rebuilds its chain by a stage revision opens again at the commit where its latest stage revision first appears, as a restart's rebuilt Mission commit is the opening of a restarted lineage. A rule set adopted in that commit is adopted at open; one adopted later is refused. A revived lineage with no stage revision, and a lineage that was not revived, keep the opening of their Mission output. Enforced by the shape that refuses a revived lineage adopting a newer rule set with no stage revision, and by the order check 1.15.0 in the release gate for the commit of the adoption; proven by backlog_revival_opening_probe (five cases; the opening case fails against order check 1.14.0)." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:RevivalAdoptionNeedsRevisionShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v156.0.0, section G192; Owner decision of 2026-11-03 02:41 Istanbul (option 1: treat the revival as the opening)." .

# ---- Ruling G193, 2026-11-03: finishes in archived history are explained row by row, never excused as a class ----
fw:Ruling_G193 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G193" ;
    rdfs:label "A finish later than the commit that recorded the item Done, in archived history, is explained by a ledger row; a new one is never excused"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The comparison of every recorded finish with the commit that first recorded the item Done still fails on any finish later than that commit. Nineteen items of the archive register carry such a finish; they are history that cannot be edited, so each is explained by one row of a ledger (item, first-Done time, finish, gap, commit, reason). A row explains an item only while all three measured values equal it; a row that explains nothing fails, so the ledger can only shrink; an item not in the ledger fails as before. The check showed the nineteen only once the clone held the history; a shallow clone hides them. Enforced by flow_point_git_trace 1.2.0 in the release gate and proven by its probe 1.1.0 (six ledger cases)." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:FlowPointsMatchHistoryShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v156.0.0, section G193; Owner decision of 2026-11-03 09:45 Istanbul (option 1: a ledger row for each of the nineteen)." .

# ---- Stage revision of Lineage 29, 2026-11-03: the chain is rebuilt from the Objective stage ----
# The revived lineage opens again at this commit (G192): it adopts here the rule set that profile revision 13 introduced.
# The outputs of the Objective and Backlog stages are retracted in this commit and kept; the rebuilt outputs follow, each in its own commit.
fw:SRev_ImpedimentsKnown a backlog:StageRevision ; rdfs:label "Stage revision of Lineage 29: the chain is rebuilt from the Objective stage"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Objective ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The objectives of Lineage 29 were all measured by the lineage's own proxy counts and none by live use, and the lineage was opened under profile revision 12, so the rule set of known obstacles never judged its work. The Mission and the Scope stand. The Objective and Backlog stages are rebuilt so that the objectives are measured on live use, the verified gaps are planned as work, and the lineage adopts the current rule sets in this commit, which is its opening again (G192). The Owner decided on 2026-11-03 to revive the lineage and rebuild its chain." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput fw:Out_Objective_ImpedimentsKnown , fw:Out_Backlog_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:Out_Objective_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:outputRetracted true .
fw:Out_Backlog_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:outputRetracted true .
fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:adoptsRuleSet backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown .
# The six work items of the first Backlog stage are older than the rebuilt chain by definition; the rebuilt Backlog output admits them.
fw:ST_IK_KindsOfObstacle backlog:preLineageItem true .
fw:ST_IK_WaysToClear backlog:preLineageItem true .
fw:ST_IK_RaiseAdviseClear backlog:preLineageItem true .
fw:T_IK_KindsOfObstacle_Build backlog:preLineageItem true .
fw:T_IK_WaysToClear_Build backlog:preLineageItem true .
fw:T_IK_RaiseAdviseClear_Build backlog:preLineageItem true .

# ---- Ruling G194, 2026-11-03: the chain is derived from the scope taxonomy; no development outside the backlog ----
fw:Ruling_G194 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G194" ;
    rdfs:label "The chain is derived from the scope taxonomy, and a governed file changes only for planned work or on a cited, dated Owner ruling"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The scope statement holds areas, deliverables and exclusions in a product or work layer; every area, kept area and exclusion is answered by a goal of its facing, the mission by a mission-facing goal, every goal is measured by objectives and each metric is derived from its goal; a gap found later becomes a scope item by a change request before it is a goal, an objective or a story. A change to an ontology, shape or tool file is the work of a planned story of a live lineage: the release gate passes it only when an item moved or when its unplanned-work line cites an Owner ruling, with the date of the decision, or an urgent interruption that the same release records; a bare declaration fails. Enforced today by release item check 1.6.0 and by OwnerRulingDatedShape; the answering of every scope item by a goal is the work of the revived Lineage 29." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v157.0.0, section G194; Owner instruction of 2026-11-03 12:40 Istanbul." .

# ---- Post-closure findings raised against Lineage 29 on 2026-11-03, after the Owner's challenge of the draft objectives ----
fw:Find_C29_ScopeTaxonomyNoParentChild a backlog:PostClosureFinding ; rdfs:label "The scope taxonomy has no parent-child link between areas, deliverables, exclusions or goals"@en ;
    backlog:declaresGapFor fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:describesUncoveredScope "The scope taxonomy classifies areas, deliverables and exclusions by layer and goals by facing, but no link arranges them as a tree: an area cannot sit under an area, a goal cannot be broken into goals, a deliverable cannot sit under a deliverable. The Owner asked on 2026-11-03 for the missing parent-child link to be added to the revived lineage as a gap from the building of the taxonomy." ;
    backlog:hasFindingScale backlog:Scale_Bounded ;
    backlog:findingRaisedAt "2026-11-03T09:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:findingEvidence fw:Ev_C29_ScopeTaxonomyNoParentChild .
fw:Ev_C29_ScopeTaxonomyNoParentChild a backlog:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Evidence for: the scope taxonomy has no parent-child link"@en ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "register T-Box v1.165.0 read: every class and property whose name or definition mentions scope, area, deliverable, exclusion or goal" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Listed the terms of the scope taxonomy (scope statement, area, deliverable, exclusion, layer, product kind, facing, goal covers area, guards exclusion, requires deliverable); none relates an area to an area, a deliverable to a deliverable, an exclusion to an exclusion or a goal to a goal. The Owner's instruction of 2026-11-03 names the link as missing." .
fw:Find_C29_BareDeclarationPassedGate a backlog:PostClosureFinding ; rdfs:label "Governed files changed on a changelog line reading Unplanned work: None"@en ;
    backlog:declaresGapFor fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:describesUncoveredScope "Releases 4.0.1, 4.0.2, 4.1.0 and 4.1.1 changed governed files with no planned item and passed the release gate on the changelog line Unplanned work: None., which the release item check accepted as a declaration. The changes of 4.0.2 and 4.1.1 were records only; those of 4.1.0 changed a tool, a shape, a gate and a probe." ;
    backlog:hasFindingScale backlog:Scale_Isolated ;
    backlog:findingRaisedAt "2026-11-03T09:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:findingEvidence fw:Ev_C29_BareDeclarationPassedGate .
fw:Ev_C29_BareDeclarationPassedGate a backlog:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Evidence for: a bare declaration passed the gate"@en ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_release_item_check 1.5.0 source read; the changelog entries of 4.0.1, 4.0.2, 4.1.0 and 4.1.1" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Read the check: with no item moved, any line starting with the unplanned-work marker passes. Read the four changelog entries: each carries the marker with the text None. The check of release 1.6.0 fails the same entries in its probe." .
fw:Find_C29_ChainFromGapListNotScope a backlog:PostClosureFinding ; rdfs:label "The rebuilt objectives were derived from a list of gaps and not from the scope taxonomy, and nothing enforces the derivation"@en ;
    backlog:declaresGapFor fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:describesUncoveredScope "The draft objectives of 2026-11-03 came from the gap list, not from scope items and their goals. The ontology asks that every area be answered by a goal, every exclusion be guarded and every goal be measured, but reports an unanswered area or unguarded exclusion only as an advisory, nothing asks that a deliverable be answered by a goal, and Lineage 29 itself has five unguarded exclusions, a kept area no scope-facing goal names and no product-layer item." ;
    backlog:hasFindingScale backlog:Scale_Bounded ;
    backlog:findingRaisedAt "2026-11-03T10:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:findingEvidence fw:Ev_C29_ChainFromGapListNotScope .
fw:Ev_C29_ChainFromGapListNotScope a backlog:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Evidence for: the chain was derived from the gap list"@en ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_validate 1.18.0 on register 1.155.0; the Lineage 29 scope and goal records read" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "The validator reports as advisories: no exclusion-facing goal guards the exclusions (Lineage 29 among them), no scope-facing goal names the kept area. The scope has four areas, four deliverables and five exclusions, the goals five, none guarding an exclusion." .

# ---- Change request: the scope of Lineage 29 grows by the verified gaps outside it (decision pending until the Backlog stage is rebuilt) ----
fw:CR_C29_ScopeGrows a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by the gaps verified against its mission that the scope does not yet hold"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "The mission is that an obstacle can be named, recorded and cleared, shown by live use. Gaps verified against it lie outside the scope: the live proof, the parent-child link of the scope taxonomy, the answering of every scope item by a goal, the preflight probe, the grantor of the reviewers' access, and the two items carried over from Lineage 28. Each becomes a scope item, a goal and an objective before it is a story. Requested by the Owner on 2026-11-03; decided when the Backlog stage is rebuilt." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_MissionMet ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Pending .


# ---- Ruling G195, 2026-11-03: work is routed before it is built (a lesson learned) ----
fw:Ruling_G195 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G195" ;
    rdfs:label "Every instruction that creates work is routed, and the route recorded, before the first file changes"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "An instruction that creates work is routed first: the live lineage's change request and chain; an urgency declared first with the urgent work in a lineage of its own; a queued lineage; or, for a change to the discipline or its rulings, the Owner's dated ruling recorded in the same release. Work built before its route is set aside and entered through the route, never backfilled. Enforced by UrgentItemStartsAfterDeclarationShape (an urgent item started before its declaration is refused) and by release item check 1.7.0 (unplanned work whose cited authority is dated after the oldest changed governed file is refused)." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:UrgentItemStartsAfterDeclarationShape , backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v157.0.0, section G195; Owner decision of 2026-11-03 14:07 Istanbul (set the cost tools aside, enter them through the urgency ceremony, and record the lesson)." .
fw:Lesson_UrgentItemStartsAfterDeclarationShape a backlog:ShapeLesson ;
    rdfs:label "Lesson of UrgentItemStartsAfterDeclarationShape"@en ;
    backlog:lessonOfShape backlog:UrgentItemStartsAfterDeclarationShape ;
    backlog:hasExperienceStatement "Urgent work was built first on the Owner's word and recorded as urgent afterwards, which the ceremony cannot tell from unplanned work and the discipline calls backfill; it was set aside and entered through the ceremony."@en ;
    backlog:inLessonFamily backlog:LessonFamily_4 ;
    backlog:learnedInSegment backlog:Segment_Execution ;
    backlog:hasProfileScope backlog:Scope_Shared ;
    backlog:hasLessonConfidence backlog:Confidence_High .
fw:Lesson_OwnerRulingDatedShape a backlog:ShapeLesson ;
    rdfs:label "Lesson of OwnerRulingDatedShape"@en ;
    backlog:lessonOfShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:hasExperienceStatement "Four releases passed the gate on the line Unplanned work: None.; unplanned work now has to cite a dated Owner ruling or an urgent interruption the release records, and the date is what lets the gate see that authority came before the work."@en ;
    backlog:inLessonFamily backlog:LessonFamily_4 ;
    backlog:learnedInSegment backlog:Segment_Execution ;
    backlog:hasProfileScope backlog:Scope_Shared ;
    backlog:hasLessonConfidence backlog:Confidence_High .

# ---- Lineage 30 (urgent): neither time nor tokens are spent twice: opening and Mission stage ----
# Opened on the Owner's instruction of 2026-11-03 13:06 Istanbul as an urgent lineage of its own; its urgency is declared when its Backlog stage has closed (the urgency tool needs the urgent item to exist).
fw:L_CostSaving a backlog:Lineage ; rdfs:label "Lineage 30: neither time nor tokens are spent twice"@en ;
    backlog:lineageOrdinal 30 ;
    backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:lineageForMission fw:Mission_CostSaving ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Backlogged ;
    backlog:hasLineageDepthLevel backlog:Depth_StoryDirect ;
    backlog:hasLineageArtifactDomain backlog:Domain_Infrastructure ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register .
fw:L_CostSaving backlog:openedWithProfile backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive ;
    backlog:openedUnderRevision backlog:Pr_13 ;
    backlog:humanApprovalLevel 3 ;
    backlog:adoptionRecordedAtOpen true ;
    backlog:adoptsRuleSet
        backlog:RS_AgentAccountability ,
        backlog:RS_CancellationAssessed ,
        backlog:RS_CeremonyKinds ,
        backlog:RS_ChainBothWays ,
        backlog:RS_ChangeSupportsMission ,
        backlog:RS_ConcurrentLineages ,
        backlog:RS_DecompositionStateAgrees ,
        backlog:RS_DigestTable_v5 ,
        backlog:RS_FlowPointsRecorded ,
        backlog:RS_ImpedimentNamesWhatItBlocks ,
        backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown ,
        backlog:RS_IndependentVerification ,
        backlog:RS_ObligationsFollowStatus ,
        backlog:RS_PlanBeforeStart ,
        backlog:RS_PlannedDates ,
        backlog:RS_ReadinessChecked ,
        backlog:RS_RepairReprioritises ,
        backlog:RS_ReviewNeedsControlRun ,
        backlog:RS_StateReflectsEvidence ,
        backlog:RS_StatusHistoryRecorded ,
        backlog:RS_VerifierSession .
fw:Mission_CostSaving a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "Mission: neither time nor tokens are spent twice"@en ;
    backlog:hasMissionOutcome backlog:Out_InFlight ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "A session spends neither time nor tokens twice: it starts from one short command that says what changed since it last read the disciplines, a fault in a changed tool or probe shows within seconds and not after the long release gate, and a gate log is read in a few lines." ;
    backlog:missionFor fw:Register ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin backlog:Origin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:missionSource "Owner, 2026-11-03 13:06 Istanbul: cost and processing saving is urgent, build the tools first; 14:07: enter them through the urgency ceremony; 14:29: a solution is needed for such long work. Measured 2026-11-03: the full release gate took 633 to 1,752 s, 68% of it in probes run two at a time, and a fault in a changed probe showed only after it; each session reads both disciplines and the ceremony output in full, thousands of unchanged lines." ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Mission_CostSaving ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:Out_Mission_CostSaving a backlog:StageOutput ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Mission ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "805101ab9b64c4bcd1bc4d146ad787459edeef220ca177da116d32bf86fe4531" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "backlog-roadmap-framework-v4.2.1 (tag; witnessed by git, not asserted)" ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Mission stage of Lineage 30, an urgent lineage of its own, opened under the agentic adaptive profile (AAL), profile revision 13. Stage 1 of 5, one release each." .

# ---- Ruling G196, 2026-11-03: closing a stage of a lineage's chain is planned work ----
fw:Ruling_G196 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G196" ;
    rdfs:label "A release that only closes a stage of a lineage's chain is planned work and passes the release check as such"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "When the only governed file a release changes is the register and the register introduces a stage output the baseline lacked, the release closes a stage of a lineage's chain, which is the lineage's own planned work, and passes the release item check as a chain stage without a declaration of unplanned work. A release that changes any other governed file, or introduces no stage output, is judged as before. Proven by probe 1.4.0 of the release item check." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v158.0.0, section G196; Owner decision of 2026-11-03 14:47 Istanbul (proceed with the urgent lineages)." .

# ---- Lineage 30: Scope stage ----
fw:Scope_CostSaving a backlog:ScopeStatement ; rdfs:label "Scope: a first look and a short reading, so that nothing is read or waited for twice"@en ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "Three tools and nothing else: (1) one command that starts a session by resolving both disciplines from origin and saying what changed since they were last read in full; (2) one command that runs first only the probes whose inputs changed; (3) one command that reads a gate log in a few lines. Each tool is proven by a probe that fails when its key behaviour is broken. The full release gate, the release path and the disciplines are not changed." ;
    backlog:scopeForMission fw:Mission_CostSaving ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Scope_CostSaving ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ;
    backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_CS_D1 , fw:Del_CS_D2 , fw:Del_CS_D3 , fw:Del_CS_D4 , fw:Del_CS_D5 , fw:Del_CS_D6 ;
    backlog:coversArea fw:Area_CS_Start , fw:Area_CS_Look , fw:Area_CS_Read , fw:Area_CS_Kept ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion fw:Ex_CS_Gate , fw:Ex_CS_Path , fw:Ex_CS_Pages , fw:Ex_CS_Packages ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Area_CS_Start a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Area 1 Start: a session begins without re-reading unchanged text"@en ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "Counted 2026-11-03: every session reads both disciplines in full (33 and 302 lines) and the ceremony output (about 60 lines), which are unchanged between most sessions; nothing says whether they changed." ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:areaLocation "03-tooling/, 04-documentation/" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Area_CS_Look a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Area 2 Look: a fault in a changed probe shows early"@en ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "Counted 2026-11-03: 63 probes run in the release gate, two at a time, 1,196 of 1,752 s of the gate; a fault in an edited probe shows only after about twenty minutes of other checks." ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:areaLocation "03-tooling/" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Area_CS_Read a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Area 3 Read: a gate log is read in a few lines"@en ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "Counted 2026-11-03: a gate log runs to 400 to 650 lines, nearly all passing checks; the failing section and the slowest sections are a few of them." ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:areaLocation "03-tooling/" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Area_CS_Kept a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Area 4 Kept: the gate, the release path and the disciplines are as they were"@en ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "The full release gate, the release path and the two disciplines are unchanged by this lineage." ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:areaLocation "03-tooling/, 04-documentation/" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Del_CS_D1 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "1.1 One command resolves both disciplines from origin by integer version and says for each: never read, unchanged since the copy read in full, or changed (it prints the difference only); it prints the ceremony verdict"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_CS_Start ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "it starts from one short command that says what changed since it last read the disciplines" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Del_CS_D2 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "2.1 One command lists and runs first the probes whose inputs changed in the working tree, or with a flag only the probes edited, and prints one line each and the tail of a failure"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_CS_Look ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "a fault in a changed tool or probe shows within seconds and not after the long release gate" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Del_CS_D3 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "2.2 The first look on a batch of edited probes ends within one minute"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_CS_Look ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_NonFunctional ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "a fault in a changed tool or probe shows within seconds" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Del_CS_D4 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "3.1 One command prints a gate log's failing sections, its three slowest sections and its verdict in about ten lines, and names the log for the full text"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_CS_Read ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "a gate log is read in a few lines" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Del_CS_D5 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "3.2 Each of the three commands is proven by a probe that fails when its key behaviour is broken, and the probe runs in the release gate"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_CS_Read ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "a fault shows early and a tool that refuses is not thereby correct" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Del_CS_D6 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "4.1 The full release gate, the release path and the two disciplines are unchanged by this lineage, and the register stays free of violation"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_CS_Kept ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "neither time nor tokens are spent twice, with nothing else changed" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Ex_CS_Gate a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Exclusion: shortening the full release gate itself"@en ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Shortening the full release gate itself; that is the remediation of long work, the next urgent lineage." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The Owner named it as a separate urgency on 2026-11-03 14:47." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Ex_CS_Path a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Exclusion: changing the steps of the release path"@en ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Changing the steps or the order of the release path." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The tools read and run beside the path and change none of it." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
fw:Ex_CS_Pages a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Exclusion: reading the GitHub pages"@en ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Reaching the GitHub pages themselves; the page fetch is refused in this environment and the tools read git." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "A measured limit of the environment, stated in the tool's text." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_CostSaving .
